{"name":"Rivers Edge","hex":"#afd9d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rivers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of river"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of river"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rivers"},{"term":"edge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The boundary line of a surface.","A one-dimensional face of a polytope. In particular, the joining line between two vertices of a polygon; the place where two faces of a polyhedron meet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move an object slowly and carefully in a particular direction.","To move slowly and carefully in a particular direction."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edge"}],"entries":[{"title":"River's Edge","blocks":[{"text":"River's Edge is a 1986 American crime drama film directed by Tim Hunter, written by Neal Jimenez, and starring Crispin Glover, Keanu Reeves, Ione Skye in her film debut, Daniel Roebuck, and Dennis Hopper. It follows a group of teenagers in a Northern California town who are forced to deal with their friend's murder of his girlfriend and the subsequent disposal of her body. Jimenez partially based the script on the 1981 murder of Marcy Renee Conrad in Milpitas, California."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Rivers-edge-poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River's_Edge"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png/500px-NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png/500px-NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The major drainage basins in North America","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Perito_Moreno_Glacier_2023.jpg/500px-Perito_Moreno_Glacier_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Perito_Moreno_Glacier_2023.jpg/1280px-Perito_Moreno_Glacier_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Perito_Moreno_Glacier_2023.jpg/500px-Perito_Moreno_Glacier_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Melting toe of the Perito Moreno Glacier in Los Glaciares National Park, Argentina","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APerito_Moreno_Glacier_2023.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Grand_Canyon_Powell_Point_Evening_Light_02_2013.jpg/500px-Grand_Canyon_Powell_Point_Evening_Light_02_20